# Cloudflare routing for the Expo Router static export.
# Expo copies everything in apps/mobile/public/ to the export root, so this file
# ships with the build automatically.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# `web.output: "static"` pre-renders one HTML file per route, but a DYNAMIC route
# can only be pre-rendered as its literal bracket filename:
#     events/[id].html      dogs/[id]/timeline.html      sessions/[id]/log.html
# A real request for /events/8f3c-... matches no file on disk -> hard 404, and the
# client router never gets a chance to run. These rules rewrite (200 = serve in
# place, do NOT redirect) each dynamic path to the shared app shell. Preserving
# the original URL is the whole point: the client router reads it to pick the
# route. A redirect would change the address bar and render the wrong screen.
#
# DESTINATION HAS NO .html EXTENSION — THIS IS DELIBERATE
# Cloudflare's default `html_handling: "auto-trailing-slash"` strips `.html` and
# issues a 307 to the extensionless path. A destination of `/app-shell.html`
# therefore gets rewritten AND THEN redirected, so the browser lands on
# /app-shell and the client router renders not-found instead of the real screen.
# Verified live on 2026-10-04:
#     /events/test-123 -> 307 Location: /app-shell
# Targeting `/app-shell` (no extension) resolves to app-shell.html with a true
# 200 and no redirect — the same way `/about` serves about.html.
#
# /app-shell.html itself is emitted by scripts/post-export.mjs as a bracket-free
# copy of the (app) client shell; all six (app) routes export byte-identical, and
# square brackets in a Cloudflare destination are not documented as supported.
#
# ORDERING: every rule below is a specific path, never a catch-all splat, so none
# of them can shadow a real pre-rendered page (notably the marketing pages, which
# must keep serving their own pre-rendered HTML for search + link previews).
# Unmatched paths fall through to not_found_handling: "404-page" (wrangler.jsonc).

/events/:id             /app-shell   200
/dogs/:id/timeline      /app-shell   200
/sessions/:id/log       /app-shell   200
